### Pattern 1: Synchronous Request-Response (REST API)

**Use Case**: Real-time queries and operations requiring immediate response.

**Architecture**:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant Service A
    participant Service B

    Client->>Service A: HTTP GET /claims/12345
    activate Service A
    Service A->>Service B: HTTP GET /payments/12345
    activate Service B
    Service B-->>Service A: Payment Data
    deactivate Service B
    Service A-->>Client: Claim + Payment Data
    deactivate Service A

    Note over Client,Service B: Synchronous blocking - client waits for complete response
```

**Implementation - ASP.NET Core REST API**:

```csharp
// Controller exposing REST endpoint
[ApiController]
[Route("api/claims")]
public class ClaimsController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly IClaimsService _claimsService;
    private readonly IHttpClientFactory _httpClientFactory;
    private readonly ILogger<ClaimsController> _logger;

    [HttpGet("{claimId}")]
    [ProducesResponseType(typeof(ClaimDetails), StatusCodes.Status200OK)]
    [ProducesResponseType(StatusCodes.Status404NotFound)]
    [ProducesResponseType(StatusCodes.Status500InternalServerError)]
    public async Task<ActionResult<ClaimDetails>> GetClaimDetails(string claimId)
    {
        try
        {
            // Retrieve claim from local database
            var claim = await _claimsService.GetClaimAsync(claimId);
            if (claim == null)
                return NotFound(new { Error = $"Claim {claimId} not found" });

            // Call downstream payment service synchronously
            var payment = await GetPaymentDetailsAsync(claimId);

            var result = new ClaimDetails
            {
                ClaimId = claim.ClaimId,
                MemberId = claim.MemberId,
                Status = claim.Status,
                PaymentInfo = payment
            };

            return Ok(result);
        }
        catch (HttpRequestException ex)
        {
            _logger.LogError(ex, "Payment service unavailable for claim {ClaimId}", claimId);
            return StatusCode(503, new { Error = "Payment service temporarily unavailable" });
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _logger.LogError(ex, "Error retrieving claim {ClaimId}", claimId);
            return StatusCode(500, new { Error = "Internal server error" });
        }
    }

    private async Task<PaymentInfo> GetPaymentDetailsAsync(string claimId)
    {
        var client = _httpClientFactory.CreateClient("PaymentService");

        // Call payment service REST API
        var response = await client.GetAsync($"/api/payments/{claimId}");
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();

        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<PaymentInfo>();
    }
}

// Resilience configuration with Polly
services.AddHttpClient("PaymentService", client =>
{
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri("https://payment-service.gainwell.com");
    client.Timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
})
.AddPolicyHandler(GetRetryPolicy())
.AddPolicyHandler(GetCircuitBreakerPolicy());

static IAsyncPolicy<HttpResponseMessage> GetRetryPolicy()
{
    return HttpPolicyExtensions
        .HandleTransientHttpError()
        .WaitAndRetryAsync(3, retryAttempt =>
            TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(100 * Math.Pow(2, retryAttempt)));
}

static IAsyncPolicy<HttpResponseMessage> GetCircuitBreakerPolicy()
{
    return HttpPolicyExtensions
        .HandleTransientHttpError()
        .CircuitBreakerAsync(5, TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30));
}
```

**Key Characteristics**:
- ✅ **Low Latency**: Direct HTTP call returns in <500ms for typical query
- ✅ **Simple Error Handling**: Immediate HTTP status code indicates success/failure
- ✅ **Easy Testing**: Standard HTTP testing tools (Postman, curl, automated tests)
- ❌ **Tight Coupling**: Caller depends on callee availability
- ❌ **Blocking**: Caller thread blocks waiting for response
- ❌ **Cascading Failures**: Downstream failures propagate to caller

**When to Use**:
- Provider portal querying claim status (needs immediate display)
- Member eligibility verification at point of service (provider waiting)
- Read operations (GET requests) fetching reference data

