### Pattern 2: Synchronous High-Performance (gRPC)

**Use Case**: High-frequency internal service-to-service communication requiring low latency and high throughput.

**Architecture**:

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[Service A] -->|gRPC<br/>HTTP/2<br/>Protobuf| B[Service B]

    style A fill:#90EE90
    style B fill:#87CEEB

    Note1[" HTTP/2 multiplexing<br/>Binary serialization<br/>Code generation"]
```

**Implementation - gRPC Service (C#)**:

```protobuf
// eligibility.proto - Protocol Buffer contract
syntax = "proto3";

option csharp_namespace = "Gainwell.Eligibility.Grpc";

package eligibility;

service EligibilityService {
    rpc VerifyEligibility (EligibilityRequest) returns (EligibilityResponse);
    rpc GetMemberDetails (MemberRequest) returns (MemberResponse);
}

message EligibilityRequest {
    string member_id = 1;
    string service_date = 2;
    string service_type_code = 3;
}

message EligibilityResponse {
    bool is_eligible = 1;
    string plan_id = 2;
    string coverage_start_date = 3;
    string coverage_end_date = 4;
    repeated string covered_services = 5;
}
```

```csharp
// Server implementation
public class EligibilityService : Eligibility.EligibilityServiceBase
{
    private readonly IEligibilityRepository _repository;
    private readonly ILogger<EligibilityService> _logger;

    public override async Task<EligibilityResponse> VerifyEligibility(
        EligibilityRequest request,
        ServerCallContext context)
    {
        var memberId = request.MemberId;
        var serviceDate = DateTime.Parse(request.ServiceDate);

        // Query eligibility from database
        var eligibility = await _repository.GetEligibilityAsync(memberId, serviceDate);

        return new EligibilityResponse
        {
            IsEligible = eligibility.IsActive,
            PlanId = eligibility.PlanId,
            CoverageStartDate = eligibility.StartDate.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd"),
            CoverageEndDate = eligibility.EndDate.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd"),
            CoveredServices = { eligibility.CoveredServices }
        };
    }
}

// Client calling gRPC service
public class ClaimsAdjudicationService
{
    private readonly EligibilityService.EligibilityServiceClient _eligibilityClient;

    public async Task<bool> ValidateEligibility(string memberId, DateTime serviceDate)
    {
        var request = new EligibilityRequest
        {
            MemberId = memberId,
            ServiceDate = serviceDate.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd"),
            ServiceTypeCode = "medical"
        };

        // Call gRPC service - strongly typed, binary protocol
        var response = await _eligibilityClient.VerifyEligibilityAsync(request);

        return response.IsEligible;
    }
}

// DI configuration
services.AddGrpcClient<EligibilityService.EligibilityServiceClient>(options =>
{
    options.Address = new Uri("https://eligibility-service.gainwell.com");
})
.ConfigurePrimaryHttpMessageHandler(() => new SocketsHttpHandler
{
    PooledConnectionIdleTimeout = Timeout.InfiniteTimeSpan,
    KeepAlivePingDelay = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(60),
    KeepAlivePingTimeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30),
    EnableMultipleHttp2Connections = true
});
```

**Key Characteristics**:
- ✅ **High Performance**: 70% smaller payloads than JSON, HTTP/2 multiplexing
- ✅ **Type Safety**: Strongly-typed contracts with code generation
- ✅ **Streaming**: Bidirectional streaming for real-time data
- ✅ **Efficient**: Binary Protocol Buffers vs. text JSON
- ❌ **Limited Browser Support**: Not directly callable from web browsers
- ❌ **Learning Curve**: Team must learn Protocol Buffers and gRPC patterns

**When to Use**:
- High-frequency internal service calls (eligibility checks during adjudication)
- Real-time streaming scenarios (claim status updates)
- Performance-critical paths (pharmacy POS needing <3 second response)

**Performance Comparison** (Eligibility Service - 10K requests):

| Metric | REST (JSON) | gRPC (Protobuf) |
|---|---|---|
| **Average Latency** | 45ms | 18ms |
| **P95 Latency** | 120ms | 35ms |
| **Payload Size** | 1.2 KB | 380 bytes |
| **CPU Usage** | 35% | 12% |
| **Network Bandwidth** | 12 MB | 3.8 MB |

