### Pattern 3: Asynchronous Message Queue (Point-to-Point)

**Use Case**: Background processing, workload distribution, and task queuing where single consumer processes each message.

**Architecture**:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Sender
    participant Queue
    participant Receiver

    Sender->>Queue: Send Message (ClaimSubmitted)
    Note over Sender: Sender continues immediately<br/>Does not wait
    Queue->>Queue: Persist Message
    Queue->>Receiver: Deliver Message
    activate Receiver
    Receiver->>Receiver: Process Claim
    Receiver->>Queue: Acknowledge (Complete)
    deactivate Receiver
    Queue->>Queue: Remove from Queue

    Note over Sender,Receiver: Asynchronous - sender and receiver decoupled
```

**Implementation - Azure Service Bus Queue**:

```csharp
// Message publisher (Claims Intake Service)
public class ClaimsIntakeService
{
    private readonly ServiceBusSender _queueSender;
    private readonly ILogger<ClaimsIntakeService> _logger;

    public async Task<ClaimSubmissionResult> SubmitClaimAsync(ClaimSubmission claim)
    {
        // Validate claim format
        var validationResult = ValidateClaim(claim);
        if (!validationResult.IsValid)
            return ClaimSubmissionResult.ValidationFailed(validationResult.Errors);

        // Create correlation ID for tracking
        var correlationId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString();

        // Create message with claim data
        var message = new ServiceBusMessage(JsonSerializer.Serialize(claim))
        {
            MessageId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString(),
            CorrelationId = correlationId,
            ContentType = "application/json",
            Subject = "ClaimSubmitted"
        };

        // Add custom properties for routing/filtering
        message.ApplicationProperties["ClaimType"] = claim.ClaimType;
        message.ApplicationProperties["Priority"] = claim.IsPriority ? "High" : "Normal";

        // Send message to queue - fire and forget
        await _queueSender.SendMessageAsync(message);

        _logger.LogInformation(
            "Claim {ClaimId} submitted to adjudication queue with correlation ID {CorrelationId}",
            claim.ClaimId, correlationId);

        // Return immediately with tracking ID - claim processed asynchronously
        return ClaimSubmissionResult.Success(correlationId);
    }
}

// Message consumer (Claims Adjudication Service)
public class ClaimsAdjudicationServiceProcessor : BackgroundService
{
    private readonly ServiceBusProcessor _processor;
    private readonly IClaimsAdjudicationService _adjudicationService;
    private readonly ILogger<ClaimsAdjudicationServiceProcessor> _logger;

    protected override async Task ExecuteAsync(CancellationToken stoppingToken)
    {
        // Register message handler
        _processor.ProcessMessageAsync += ProcessClaimMessageAsync;
        _processor.ProcessErrorAsync += ErrorHandler;

        // Start processing messages from queue
        await _processor.StartProcessingAsync(stoppingToken);

        // Keep running until cancellation requested
        await Task.Delay(Timeout.Infinite, stoppingToken);
    }

    private async Task ProcessClaimMessageAsync(ProcessMessageEventArgs args)
    {
        var message = args.Message;
        var correlationId = message.CorrelationId;

        try
        {
            // Deserialize claim from message body
            var claim = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<ClaimSubmission>(message.Body.ToString());

            _logger.LogInformation(
                "Processing claim {ClaimId} with correlation ID {CorrelationId}",
                claim.ClaimId, correlationId);

            // Adjudicate claim (may take 30-60 seconds)
            var result = await _adjudicationService.AdjudicateClaimAsync(claim);

            // Complete message - removes from queue
            await args.CompleteMessageAsync(args.Message);

            _logger.LogInformation(
                "Successfully adjudicated claim {ClaimId} with result {Result}",
                claim.ClaimId, result.Decision);
        }
        catch (JsonException ex)
        {
            _logger.LogError(ex, "Invalid message format for correlation ID {CorrelationId}", correlationId);

            // Dead letter message - moves to DLQ for manual review
            await args.DeadLetterMessageAsync(args.Message, "InvalidFormat", ex.Message);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _logger.LogError(ex, "Error processing claim with correlation ID {CorrelationId}", correlationId);

            // Abandon message - will be redelivered after visibility timeout
            await args.AbandonMessageAsync(args.Message);
        }
    }

    private Task ErrorHandler(ProcessErrorEventArgs args)
    {
        _logger.LogError(args.Exception, "Error in message processor: {ErrorSource}", args.ErrorSource);
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }
}

// Configuration in Program.cs
builder.Services.AddSingleton(sp =>
{
    var connectionString = builder.Configuration["AzureServiceBus:ConnectionString"];
    return new ServiceBusClient(connectionString);
});

builder.Services.AddSingleton(sp =>
{
    var client = sp.GetRequiredService<ServiceBusClient>();
    return client.CreateSender("claims-adjudication-queue");
});

builder.Services.AddSingleton(sp =>
{
    var client = sp.GetRequiredService<ServiceBusClient>();
    return client.CreateProcessor("claims-adjudication-queue", new ServiceBusProcessorOptions
    {
        MaxConcurrentCalls = 10,
        AutoCompleteMessages = false,
        MaxAutoLockRenewalDuration = TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5)
    });
});
```

**Key Characteristics**:
- ✅ **Temporal Decoupling**: Sender continues immediately without waiting
- ✅ **Load Leveling**: Queue buffers spikes, consumer processes at sustainable rate
- ✅ **Guaranteed Delivery**: Message persisted, survives crashes
- ✅ **Fault Tolerance**: Receiver failures don't affect sender
- ✅ **Scalability**: Multiple consumers process messages in parallel
- ❌ **Eventual Processing**: Message not processed immediately
- ❌ **Complexity**: Dead letter queue handling, idempotency required

**When to Use**:
- Claims adjudication workflow (submit and process asynchronously)
- Provider credentialing background checks (long-running operations)
- Report generation (30-60 minute processing time)
- Batch processing (nightly eligibility file imports)

