### Pattern 5: Hybrid Request-Response with Async Backend

**Use Case**: Long-running operations where caller needs tracking ID but doesn't need immediate result.

**Implementation - HTTP 202 Accepted Pattern**:

```csharp
// Controller accepting long-running request
[ApiController]
[Route("api/providers")]
public class ProviderEnrollmentController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly ServiceBusSender _queueSender;
    private readonly IProviderRepository _repository;

    [HttpPost("credentialing")]
    [ProducesResponseType(typeof(CredentialingTrackingResponse), StatusCodes.Status202Accepted)]
    public async Task<IActionResult> SubmitCredentialingApplication(
        [FromBody] CredentialingApplication application)
    {
        // Validate application
        var validationResult = Validate(application);
        if (!validationResult.IsValid)
            return BadRequest(validationResult.Errors);

        // Generate tracking ID
        var trackingId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString();

        // Store application in database with "Pending" status
        await _repository.CreateApplicationAsync(trackingId, application, "Pending");

        // Submit to background queue for processing
        var message = new ServiceBusMessage(JsonSerializer.Serialize(application))
        {
            MessageId = trackingId,
            ContentType = "application/json"
        };
        await _queueSender.SendMessageAsync(message);

        // Return 202 Accepted with tracking ID and status check URL
        var response = new CredentialingTrackingResponse
        {
            TrackingId = trackingId,
            Status = "Pending",
            StatusUrl = $"/api/providers/credentialing/{trackingId}/status",
            EstimatedCompletionMinutes = 60
        };

        return AcceptedAtAction(
            nameof(GetCredentialingStatus),
            new { trackingId },
            response);
    }

    [HttpGet("credentialing/{trackingId}/status")]
    [ProducesResponseType(typeof(CredentialingStatusResponse), StatusCodes.Status200OK)]
    [ProducesResponseType(StatusCodes.Status404NotFound)]
    public async Task<ActionResult<CredentialingStatusResponse>> GetCredentialingStatus(string trackingId)
    {
        var application = await _repository.GetApplicationAsync(trackingId);
        if (application == null)
            return NotFound();

        var response = new CredentialingStatusResponse
        {
            TrackingId = trackingId,
            Status = application.Status, // Pending, InProgress, Approved, Denied
            SubmittedDate = application.SubmittedDate,
            LastUpdated = application.LastUpdated,
            CompletionPercentage = CalculateProgress(application),
            CurrentStep = application.CurrentStep
        };

        return Ok(response);
    }
}
```

**Key Characteristics**:
- ✅ **Immediate Response**: API returns 202 Accepted immediately with tracking ID
- ✅ **Non-Blocking**: Backend processes asynchronously without blocking API worker
- ✅ **Status Tracking**: Client can poll status endpoint or receive webhook notification
- ✅ **Resource Efficiency**: Doesn't hold HTTP connections during long processing
- ❌ **Polling Overhead**: Client must repeatedly poll for status updates
- ❌ **Complexity**: Requires status tracking database and background worker

**When to Use**:
- Provider credentialing (30 minutes - 2 hours processing)
- Report generation (5-30 minutes)
- Bulk data exports (1-10 minutes)
- File uploads with validation and processing

