### Example 2: Member Eligibility Updates - Event-Driven Pattern

**Business Context**:
State agencies send eligibility files with 10K+ member updates daily. Multiple Gainwell systems must react: Claims Processing, Member Portal, ID Card Service, Provider Directory, Care Management. Original synchronous orchestration took 8 hours and created system inconsistencies when any service failed.

**Solution**: Event-driven pub-sub pattern with `MemberEligibilityChanged` event.

**Architecture**:

```mermaid
graph TB
    StateFile[State Agency<br/>Eligibility File] --> FileProcessor[File Processor]
    FileProcessor --> EligibilityDB[(Eligibility<br/>Database)]
    FileProcessor --> EventTopic[MemberEligibilityChanged<br/>Event Topic]

    EventTopic --> Sub1[Claims Service<br/>Subscription]
    EventTopic --> Sub2[Member Portal<br/>Subscription]
    EventTopic --> Sub3[ID Card Service<br/>Subscription]
    EventTopic --> Sub4[Provider Directory<br/>Subscription]
    EventTopic --> Sub5[Care Management<br/>Subscription]

    Sub1 --> Claims[Update Adjudication Rules]
    Sub2 --> Portal[Update Member Profile]
    Sub3 --> IDCard[Generate New Card]
    Sub4 --> Directory[Update Relationships]
    Sub5 --> Care[Update Care Team]
```

**Implementation**:

```csharp
// Event publisher - Eligibility File Processor
public class EligibilityFileProcessor
{
    public async Task ProcessEligibilityFileAsync(EligibilityFile file)
    {
        foreach (var update in file.MemberUpdates)
        {
            // Update eligibility database
            var oldEligibility = await _repository.GetEligibilityAsync(update.MemberId);
            await _repository.UpdateEligibilityAsync(update);

            // Publish event - all subscribers receive independently
            await _eventPublisher.PublishAsync(new MemberEligibilityChangedEvent
            {
                EventId = Guid.NewGuid().ToString(),
                EventTimestamp = DateTime.UtcNow,
                MemberId = update.MemberId,
                OldPlanId = oldEligibility.PlanId,
                NewPlanId = update.PlanId,
                EffectiveDate = update.EffectiveDate,
                ChangeReason = "State Agency Update"
            });

            _logger.LogInformation(
                "Published eligibility change for member {MemberId}: {OldPlan} → {NewPlan}",
                update.MemberId, oldEligibility.PlanId, update.PlanId);
        }
    }
}

// Event subscriber - Claims Service
public class ClaimsEligibilityHandler : IEventHandler<MemberEligibilityChangedEvent>
{
    public async Task HandleAsync(MemberEligibilityChangedEvent evt)
    {
        _logger.LogInformation(
            "Processing eligibility change for member {MemberId} in Claims Service",
            evt.MemberId);

        // Update adjudication rules for new plan
        await _claimsConfig.UpdateMemberPlanAsync(evt.MemberId, evt.NewPlanId);

        // Reprocess any pending claims for this member
        await _claimsProcessor.ReprocessPendingClaimsAsync(evt.MemberId);
    }
}

// Event subscriber - ID Card Service
public class IdCardEligibilityHandler : IEventHandler<MemberEligibilityChangedEvent>
{
    public async Task HandleAsync(MemberEligibilityChangedEvent evt)
    {
        _logger.LogInformation(
            "Generating new ID card for member {MemberId}",
            evt.MemberId);

        try
        {
            // Generate new ID card PDF (2 seconds)
            var card = await _idCardService.GenerateCardAsync(
                evt.MemberId,
                evt.NewPlanId,
                evt.EffectiveDate);

            // Send to print vendor
            await _printVendor.SubmitForPrintingAsync(card);
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            // ID card failure doesn't affect other subscribers
            _logger.LogError(ex, "Failed to generate ID card for member {MemberId}", evt.MemberId);
            // Dead letter for manual review
            throw;
        }
    }
}
```

**Results**:
- **Processing Time**: 30 minutes (from 8 hours) - parallel subscriber processing
- **System Consistency**: 100% consistency (each subscriber processes independently)
- **Resilience**: ID Card Service failures don't affect Claims or Portal updates
- **Extensibility**: Added Care Management subscriber without modifying publisher (zero code changes)
- **Event Lag**: P95 <30 seconds from publication to all subscribers complete
- **Operational Efficiency**: Zero manual data sync issues (200+ tickets/month eliminated)

