### Example 3: Provider Portal Claim Query - Synchronous with Optimization

**Business Context**:
Provider portal "View Claim" page aggregates data from 4 services (Claims, Payment, Prior Auth, Eligibility). Original sequential synchronous calls created P95 latency of 3.2 seconds, frustrating providers. Goal: <1 second for 95% of requests.

**Solution**: Parallel synchronous calls with fallback for non-critical data.

**Architecture**:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Provider
    participant Portal
    participant Claims
    participant Payment
    participant PriorAuth
    participant Eligibility

    Provider->>Portal: GET /claims/12345
    activate Portal

    par Parallel Calls
        Portal->>Claims: GET /claims/12345
        Portal->>Payment: GET /payments?claimId=12345
        Portal->>PriorAuth: GET /authorizations?claimId=12345
        Portal->>Eligibility: GET /eligibility/{memberId}
    end

    Claims-->>Portal: Claim Details (200ms)
    Payment-->>Portal: Payment Info (300ms)
    PriorAuth--xPortal: 503 Service Unavailable
    Eligibility-->>Portal: Member Info (400ms)

    Portal->>Portal: Aggregate Results<br/>Fallback for PriorAuth
    Portal-->>Provider: Claim Details (400ms total)
    deactivate Portal

    Note over Provider,Eligibility: Total latency = max(200,300,timeout,400) = 400ms<br/>Not sum(200+300+timeout+400)
```

**Implementation**:

```csharp
[HttpGet("claims/{claimId}")]
public async Task<ActionResult<ClaimDetailsViewModel>> GetClaimDetails(string claimId)
{
    // Parallel execution - wait for all or timeout
    var claimTask = _claimsClient.GetClaimAsync(claimId);
    var paymentTask = _paymentClient.GetPaymentAsync(claimId);
    var priorAuthTask = _priorAuthClient.GetAuthorizationAsync(claimId)
        .WithFallback(null); // Non-critical data - continue if fails
    var eligibilityTask = GetEligibilityWithClaimAsync(claimTask);

    // Wait for all tasks (runs in parallel)
    await Task.WhenAll(
        claimTask,
        paymentTask,
        priorAuthTask,
        eligibilityTask);

    // Aggregate results
    var claim = await claimTask;
    if (claim == null)
        return NotFound();

    var viewModel = new ClaimDetailsViewModel
    {
        ClaimId = claim.ClaimId,
        ServiceDate = claim.ServiceDate,
        Status = claim.Status,
        ProviderId = claim.ProviderId,

        // Critical data
        PaymentInfo = await paymentTask,
        MemberEligibility = await eligibilityTask,

        // Non-critical - may be null if service unavailable
        PriorAuthorization = await priorAuthTask
    };

    return Ok(viewModel);
}

private async Task<Eligibility> GetEligibilityWithClaimAsync(Task<Claim> claimTask)
{
    var claim = await claimTask;
    if (claim == null) return null;

    return await _eligibilityClient.GetEligibilityAsync(
        claim.MemberId,
        claim.ServiceDate);
}

// Extension method for fallback
public static async Task<T> WithFallback<T>(this Task<T> task, T fallbackValue)
{
    try
    {
        return await task;
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        _logger.LogWarning(ex, "Operation failed, using fallback value");
        return fallbackValue;
    }
}

// HTTP client configuration with aggressive timeout
services.AddHttpClient<IPriorAuthClient, PriorAuthClient>(client =>
{
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri(configuration["Services:PriorAuth:Url"]);
    client.Timeout = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(800); // Aggressive timeout for non-critical
})
.AddPolicyHandler(Policy<HttpResponseMessage>
